# Contributing to {{REPO_NAME}}

Read first: `../{{DOCS_REPO}}/docs/onboarding.md`, then `AGENTS.md`, `docs/rules/`, `../{{DOCS_REPO}}/GLOSSARY.md` and ADRs.

## Workflow
- Pick an issue labelled `ready-for-agent` or `ready-for-human`; assign yourself.
- Branch from `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` (`feat/…`, `fix/…`, `chore/…`), open a PR with `Closes #n`. Never push to `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`.
- API changes are contract-first: `{{CONTRACT_PATH}}`, then the handler (skill `add-endpoint`).
- No secrets, `.env` files or personal data in commits, issues, PRs or AI chats.

## Commands
```sh
{{BUILD_CMD}}
{{TEST_CMD}}
{{INTEGRATION_CMD}}
{{LINT_CMD}}
{{SECURITY_CMD}}
```

## Required checks
`lint`, `test`, `integration`, `security`. Image build and deploy run only after all pass in the same run (see `docs/agents/ci-skeleton.yml`).

## Migrations
Forward-only and backward compatible with the running release (skill `add-migration`).

## Editing agents
Edit only `agents/<name>.md`, run `python3 scripts/sync-agents.py`, commit the generated `.opencode/agents/` and `.github/agents/`. See `docs/agents/how-to-use-agents.md`.
